#: ../../../reference/administration/distribution-support.md:10
msgid ""
"We use a third-party tool called [Repology](https://repology.org/) to track "
"snapd version numbers across various Linux distributions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/distribution-support.md:12
msgid ""
"On some distributions, a non-snap package will install the snapd snap which "
"will subsequently update itself. This process is called _re-execution_. On "
"such systems, Repology can only detect the version number of the native non-"
"snap package and not the updated snapd from the snap."
msgstr ""

